Adaptation: Go implementation of the sequence-parallel region protocol for
fak's native engine (internal/model/tensor_parallel_sequence.go). Ported
mechanisms, in upstream terms:

  - scatter_to_sequence_parallel_region: split the activation along the
    FIRST (sequence) dimension across tensor-parallel ranks; each rank keeps
    its contiguous band (_split_along_first_dim).
  - gather_from_sequence_parallel_region: AllGather the per-rank sequence
    bands in rank order before a tensor-parallel core
    (_gather_along_first_dim).
  - reduce_scatter_to_sequence_parallel_region: after a row-parallel core,
    ReduceScatter the per-rank partials back to sequence bands
    (_reduce_scatter_along_first_dim).

Divergences (fak adaptation, documented in the port file header):

  - fak's reduce-scatter is COMPOSED as AllReduceSum (the existing rank-order
    sum) followed by an ordered slice, byte-identical to a real ReduceScatter
    by the identity pinned in internal/compute/collective.go (ReduceScatter
    reuses the identical rank-order sum and slices it). The device seam
    (compute.CollectiveBackend) exposes a real ReduceScatter for the swap-in.
  - fak's validated TPPlan tiling (near-even contiguous bands, remainder on
    the first shards) replaces upstream's exact-divisibility assert on the
    first dimension.
  - Inference forward only: upstream's autograd backward pairings (gather's
    backward reduce-scatter, etc.) are not ported — fak has no training path.
  - fak materializes full-sequence activation snapshots for its Activations
    witness bookkeeping by concatenating the per-rank bands in rank order; a
    real deployment keeps the bands resident (the memory win is a deployment
    property, not observable in the single-box witness).
